  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1145 PM CST Wed Nov 4 2026\n\nA weak disturbance will move through the area overnight into the \nmorning bringing a a good chance of precipitation across the CWA. \nThe exception to this will be our 6 northern zones where \nprecipitation will not be found. Precipitation chances come to an \nend from west to east tomorrow morning. Rain fall amounts of up to a \nhalf of an inch are possible but most places should receive less \nthan a quarter of an inch. Skies will be mostly cloudy overnight \nthrough much of the day with clearing from west to east this \nafternoon. Mostly clear skies are expected for the first half of \ntonight with some mid to high level clouds after midnight into \nFriday. Winds will generally be form a northerly direction today, \nbecoming light and variable tonight into Friday. As for \ntemperatures, lows this morning look to range from the upper 30s \nalong the I-70 corridor to mid 40s across south central Kansas. \nHighs this afternoon look to only reach into the 50s due to the \nample cloud cover and cold air advection. Lows tonight will \ngenerally fall into the 30s with below freezing across our western \nhalf. Highs Friday will reach into the 50s. The NBM then keeps \nwestern Kansas dry through the remain of the forecast with high \npressure being the dominate feature at the surface. Highs during \nthis time frame will generally be in the 60s wit",
